.Dd August 20, 2026
.Dt FILEES-CLIENT-ENTRY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-client-entry
.Nd FileES per-key dispatcher for svnserve, control and Whale sessions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the set-id dispatcher installed for installation-key sessions.
.Xr sshd 8
selects the account
.Pq Sy _filees-client
or
.Sy _filees-data
and the per-key
.Ic command=
line.
.Nm
accepts exactly three original commands:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm svnserve -t
Tunnel-mode Subversion.
.It Cm filees control-v1
One authenticated control-plane ticket, then
.Xr filees-worker 8 .
.It Cm filees whale-v1
One framed Whale request.
The dispatcher claims the same activation
session lease used for Subversion, starts a gated worker in a separate
process group and relays only private pipes.
Revocation closes the input
and terminates the complete worker process group, including a running
.Cm svnmucc .
.El
.Pp
Before a control-plane ticket or Whale request it runs
.Xr filees-service-wc-corrector 8
so a previous root-owned administrative
.Nm svn
cannot leave the service working copy unreadable to
.Sy _filees-state .
.Pp
The client identity is taken only from the forced per-key command line.
It is never accepted from the Whale frame.
The Whale worker authorizes
the logical repository against the current client projection and stores
transport state outside every working copy.
.Pp
The image is
.Sy _filees-state : _filees-access
mode 4550.
It is not a general shell.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-service-wc-corrector 8 ,
.Xr filees-worker 8
